{"id":"89306cf1-f386-4ab2-9cea-b6974eea41cb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/change-problems.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"11023d74517c269c487d82545b859dabe3986344","start":31,"end":77},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"181743145324f9ca"}},"payload":{"text":"A change's problems in the review panel (git-panel.tsx places them on each changed file's row): the problems the change\nmade in it and the ones it fixed, against HEAD — TypeScript's and ESLint's, as `code.problems` compares them\n(workbench/code-problems.ts), the answer agents' `code_problems` gets. Asked again once the changes settle\n(`git.changed`), one request at a time: a comparison checks each changed file and its importers twice.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:56:31.978Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:56:31.978Z"}
